WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.268
Hi, I'm Corvin.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.225
Depth should make a model smarter.

00:00:04.225 --> 00:00:06.508
This benchmark asks when it actually does.

00:00:08.017 --> 00:00:09.797
So here is the finding.

00:00:09.797 --> 00:00:13.712
Whether depth pays off depends almost entirely on the residual connection.

00:00:15.442 --> 00:00:19.051
Until now, every residual design was tested its own way, so you

00:00:19.051 --> 00:00:20.254
could not compare them.

00:00:20.674 --> 00:00:23.703
Fix the parameter count, the data and the recipe.

00:00:23.703 --> 00:00:26.058
Change only one thing: width versus depth.

00:00:27.833 --> 00:00:31.005
A token enters at the embedding and climbs the stack.

00:00:31.005 --> 00:00:33.225
Every block adds into one shared vector.

00:00:33.645 --> 00:00:36.609
In plain pre-layer-norm, the deep blocks barely change it.

00:00:36.609 --> 00:00:38.585
They only polish a near-finished vector.

00:00:38.585 --> 00:00:40.562
That is the curse of depth.

00:00:40.982 --> 00:00:45.540
Hyper-connections and attention residuals let each block read every earlier layer, so

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.820
deep blocks keep doing real work.

00:00:49.508 --> 00:00:53.342
In plain pre-layer-norm, every layer just pours into one stream.

00:00:53.342 --> 00:00:55.260
Nothing selects an earlier layer.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:00.181
Attention residuals let a layer reach back and read specific earlier outputs,

00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:01.681
like attention across depth.

00:01:02.101 --> 00:01:06.878
Hyper-connections route through four streams, strong nearby but still reaching far back.

00:01:08.717 --> 00:01:10.222
Here is the whole result.

00:01:10.222 --> 00:01:13.834
Lower is better, and moving left makes the model deeper and narrower.

00:01:14.254 --> 00:01:18.500
Hyper-connections and attention residuals keep dropping into the deep end.

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:20.622
Plain pre-layer-norm turns and rises.

00:01:22.217 --> 00:01:26.600
When you compose its maps, the constrained version collapses toward a single direction.

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.634
The fix that gave it stability erased the gain.

00:01:31.142 --> 00:01:34.601
Depth is a real scaling axis, but only with the right residual

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:36.907
stream, and you pay for it in memory.

00:01:39.525 --> 00:01:42.930
So depth can scale, but only the right residual stream makes

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:44.169
the deep layers count.

00:01:44.589 --> 00:01:46.734
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:47.346
I'm Corvin.

00:01:47.346 --> 00:01:47.653
Bye!
